  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia-Vietnam Human Rights Technical Cooperation Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment is managed by the Australian Human Rights Commission (AHRC) and is aimed at promoting the protection of human rights in Vietnam via education, and within the private and public sector. The Program supports three primary outcomes: (i) primary, secondary, and tertiary students have increased knowledge and understanding of human rights; (ii) businesses are better equipped to act responsibly; and (iii) government officials and members of the public are better able to protect human rights online. Each respective outcome will be implemented in cooperation with a key local partner: the Vietnam Chamber of Commerce and Industry for responsible business practices, the Ho Chi Minh Political Academy for better human rights education in schools, and the Institute for Policy Studies and Media Development for the promotion of human rights online and in the public sector.</narrative>
  </description>
